@* Plan A04 (pass 28b): a SW transferred, dropped, Recovered, dismantled, or assembled. The page gives the weapons and units the view sees (ruling R23.1);
   choosing another weapon clears the unit, which the page does in its OnWeapon handler (section 15.3). The planner decides each action. *@
<h4>Support weapons</h4>
<RuleHelp Id="sw-help" Summary="A SW passes between Good Order unpinned units in one Location in the RPh or at the start of the ATTACKER's APh; it may be dropped before its unit moves or advances; it is Recovered on a Final dr below 6 (A4.43, A4.431, A4.44).">
    A SW passes between Good Order unpinned units in one Location in the RPh, or in the ATTACKER's APh before either advances (A4.431). A unit
    drops one in its MPh before it moves, its APh before it advances, or at the start of the CCPh; a broken unit, before it routs, drops what it
    cannot carry (A4.43, A10.4). A Good Order unit Recovers an unpossessed SW in its Location on a dr below 6 (+1 CX), as its sole RPh action or
    for one MF in its MPh (A4.44). The German MMG is dismantled or assembled in its side's PFPh or DFPh instead of firing; dismantled, it is not
    fired and weighs half (A9.8). A MG of the enemy's nationality fires with its B# two lower and its ROF one lower (A21.11, A21.12).
</RuleHelp>
<div class="toolbar">
    <label>
        SW
        <select id="sw-weapon" value="@Weapon" @onchange="@(args => OnWeapon.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var weapon in Weapons)
            {
                <option value="@weapon.Id">@Say(weapon.Label)</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <label>
        Recovering or receiving unit
        <select id="sw-unit" value="@Unit" @onchange="@(args => OnUnit.InvokeAsync(args.Value as string ?? string.Empty))">
            <option value="">choose</option>
            @foreach (var unit in Units)
            {
                <option value="@unit.Id">@Say(unit.Label)</option>
            }
        </select>
    </label>
    <button id="propose-transfer" disabled="@(!Held || Unit.Length == 0)" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync(Transfer))">Propose: transfer</button>
    <button id="propose-drop" disabled="@(!Held)" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync(Drop))">Propose: drop</button>
    <button id="propose-recover" disabled="@(Held || Weapon.Length == 0 || Unit.Length == 0)" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync(Recover))">Propose: recover</button>
    <button id="propose-dismantle" disabled="@(!Held || !Dismantles)" @onclick="@(() => OnPropose.InvokeAsync(Dismantle))">Propose: dismantle or assemble</button>
    <span id="sw-ready" class="toolbar-note">Transfer and drop take a SW a unit holds; recover takes a SW lying in the Location and the unit that recovers it; the game dismantles and assembles only the German MMG, in its side's Prep Fire or Defensive Fire Phase (A9.8).</span>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The page's words for the view (pass 31c, design D11): a unit's name for its id, a Location in words.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter(Name = "Say")]
    public Func<string, string>? Words { get; set; }

    private string Say(string? text) => text is null ? string.Empty : Words?.Invoke(text) ?? text;

    /// <summary>The actions the panel asks for; the page maps each to its registered action.</summary>
    public const string Transfer = "transfer";
    public const string Drop = "drop";
    public const string Recover = "recover";
    public const string Dismantle = "dismantle";

    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Weapons { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The units in the chosen weapon's Location that may receive or Recover it.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<PlayChoice> Units { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string Weapon { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Parameter]
    public string Unit { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Whether a unit possesses the chosen weapon, so it may be transferred, dropped, or dismantled.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Held { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the game dismantles or assembles the chosen SW now (pass 31, play test P-19; A9.8; ruling R13.6).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Dismantles { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnWeapon { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnUnit { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnPropose { get; set; }
}
